Subject: [PATCH] [mlir] sccp: keep the constants the IR already holds

composite-fixed-point-pass with sccp in its pipeline never converges: on
a module at its fixpoint it runs the pipeline max-iterations times and
warns. It decides convergence by OperationFingerPrint, a hash of object
identity, and sccp remakes every constant it meets even when it
propagates nothing: a constant's own result has a constant lattice, and
the OperationFolder that rewrite() creates fresh is never told about the
constants the IR already holds, so getOrCreateConstant materializes a new
one, the uses move to it and the original is erased. The module prints
the same, but every constant has a new address.
-mlir-print-ir-after-change prints after sccp for the same reason.

rewrite() now gives the folder each ConstantLike operation it meets
(insertKnownConstant), as the greedy driver does before it rewrites
anything, and moves on: every later getOrCreateConstant of that value
returns it, and a run that propagates nothing changes nothing.

Test: sccp-fixed-point.mlir, the composite pass over sccp converging in
one run without warning.
---
 mlir/lib/Transforms/SCCP.cpp               |  9 +++++++++
 mlir/test/Transforms/sccp-fixed-point.mlir | 13 +++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mlir/lib/Transforms/SCCP.cpp b/mlir/lib/Transforms/SCCP.cpp
index 471fa64e78574df0f130fdbc9086411e4fbfb6d9..1329ede6ac7b71e8b2bdc154c9839eff8af0459f 100644
--- a/mlir/lib/Transforms/SCCP.cpp
+++ b/mlir/lib/Transforms/SCCP.cpp
@@ -82,6 +82,15 @@ static void rewrite(DataFlowSolver &solver, MLIRContext *context,
     Block *block = worklist.pop_back_val();
 
     for (Operation &op : llvm::make_early_inc_range(*block)) {
+      // A constant the IR already holds is the one the folder hands out for
+      // its value, as the greedy driver does, so that a run that propagates
+      // nothing leaves the IR as it was instead of remaking every constant.
+      // The folder may hoist it, or erase it for an equal one it knows.
+      if (op.hasTrait<OpTrait::ConstantLike>()) {
+        folder.insertKnownConstant(&op);
+        continue;
+      }
+
       builder.setInsertionPoint(&op);
 
       // Replace any result with constants.
diff --git a/mlir/test/Transforms/sccp-fixed-point.mlir b/mlir/test/Transforms/sccp-fixed-point.mlir
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a165365cf636fc1fcc43936624bd2633e1195a60
--- /dev/null
+++ b/mlir/test/Transforms/sccp-fixed-point.mlir
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+// RUN: mlir-opt %s --composite-fixed-point-pass='pipeline=sccp max-iterations=1' -verify-diagnostics | FileCheck %s
+
+// sccp leaves a function it propagates nothing in as it was, its constants
+// included, so the composite pass sees the same fingerprint after one run
+// and converges without warning.
+
+// CHECK-LABEL: func @one
+// CHECK-NEXT:    arith.constant 1 : i32
+// CHECK-NEXT:    return
+func.func @one() -> i32 {
+  %c = arith.constant 1 : i32
+  return %c : i32
+}
